            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-  Receptacles

-  Old windows

-  Exterior doors (Garage and back door)

-  Furnace chimney

- Combustion air supply

- Bathroom fans

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <foundation>FOUNDATION

Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  



PONY WALL

The basement wall is composed of a 4????????? concrete blocks wall and a 2x4 frame wall (pony wall) built above the concrete foundation wall. At the time of the assessment, the concrete foundation wall was not insulated, but the pony wall insulation was R-12. No insulation on the foundation wall represents a high level of heat loss. Even if the pony wall insulation level is not enough and does not meet the actual city standard. We recommend the insulation of the basement. We recommend the insulation of the concrete wall and the pony wall to meet the city of Whitehorse standard.



The incentives for the addition of insulation are as follow:



ADDITION OF :



R-20 - R-29: $ 2.50/ square foot

R-30+         : $ 3.50/ square foot

</foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem />
                <AdditionalComments>The depressurization test performed as shown a high risk of combustion gas spillage. Therefore, we recommend verifying your carbon monoxide detectors regularly.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
